# The .NET runtime that ships in the APK.
#
# One official Microsoft package supplies everything the device needs from the
# runtime side: libcoreclr.so, libclrjit.so, the platform PAL shims and the BCL.
# Taking all four from one package is what makes the "same build" requirement in
# provenance/SOURCES.md true by construction rather than by discipline — a
# managed assembly from a different runtime build than the native engine is a
# load-time failure nothing else in the tree would catch.
#
# Changing the runtime major version touches this file and one other:
# scripts/package_bepinex_android.sh writes a runtimeconfig.json with a hardcoded
# tfm and framework version, and it has to name the same framework dotnet.zip
# provides. verify_dotnet_pack.sh only checks dotnet.zip, so a stale value in the
# runtimeconfig would not fail any gate -- it would just be wrong.
#
#   1. Update DOTNET_RUNTIME_VERSION, DOTNET_RUNTIME_TFM,
#      DOTNET_RUNTIME_EXPECTED_TFM and DOTNET_RUNTIME_PACK_SHA256 here.
#      (builds.dotnet.microsoft.com/dotnet/release-metadata/releases-index.json
#      lists `latest-runtime` per channel; the SHA-256 comes from the official
#      NuGet flat container and must be updated in the same commit.)
#   2. Update the matching tfm/version pair in scripts/package_bepinex_android.sh.
#   3. Run scripts/fetch_dotnet_runtime.sh, then regenerate
#      provenance/sha256sums.txt with
#      launcher/scripts/verify_prebuilts.sh --update-manifest.
#
# This is a GA build on the LTS line, not a release candidate. It was chosen over
# 11.0.0-rc.1 for one measured reason, recorded in docs/progress.md stage 10:
# MonoMod.Core's runtime dispatch is an explicit `switch (version.Major)` whose
# cases stop at 10 and whose default branch throws PlatformNotSupportedException,
# so every published MonoMod.Core except the 1.4.0 prerelease refuses to run on
# .NET 11. The managed stack this project needs is the XtraCube "-star" fork (it
# carries the IL2CPP/Android adaptation) and that feed is no longer published, so
# there is no 11-capable "-star" build to move to. .NET 10 is accepted by the
# pinned MonoMod.Core 1.3.4-star unchanged.
#
# Going back to 10 is NOT the source cross-build that stage 5 rejected. That
# rejection rested on the premise that Microsoft published no CoreCLR Android
# runtime pack for the .NET 10 line, which is false: this package id has shipped
# 10.0.0 through 10.0.12 on nuget.org, each with libcoreclr.so, libclrjit.so, the
# platform PALs and a net10.0 BCL. The same fetch path that produces dotnet.zip
# today produces it here, so the "BCL and native engine from one immutable
# package" property that stage 3 was about is preserved.

# The package id and version, both of which are also the cache directory name
# under the NuGet v3 flat container.
DOTNET_RUNTIME_PACK=microsoft.netcore.app.runtime.android-arm64
DOTNET_RUNTIME_VERSION=10.0.12

# SHA-256 of the .nupkg as served by https://api.nuget.org/v3-flatcontainer.
# A NuGet package is immutable once published, so this pins the exact bytes.
DOTNET_RUNTIME_PACK_SHA256=7f67905e5e5324e0c2b03920b62a3b09c036737ba84f9e7cb61f7e058d285ad3

# Target framework of the framework assemblies inside the pack. dotnet.zip is
# assembled from lib/$DOTNET_RUNTIME_TFM, and verify_dotnet_pack.sh asserts the
# pack's TargetFrameworkAttribute against DOTNET_RUNTIME_EXPECTED_TFM.
DOTNET_RUNTIME_TFM=net10.0
DOTNET_RUNTIME_EXPECTED_TFM=v10.0